@startuml UC-SUBTASK-COMPLETE
' UC-27.4 - Complete Subtask | semantic key: UC-SUBTASK-COMPLETE
' Source: data/use_cases/sprint-work/UC-SUBTASK-COMPLETE.yml
' Business Rules: BR-SPRINT-TASK-ACTIVE-SPRINT, BR-SPRINT-TASK-DEVELOPER, BR-WORK-ITEM-STATUS
' Trace comments ' [ref] name the YAML element behind the next action.
' No title: the Word caption supplies it.
' The Developer requests one of two status changes: mark an incomplete subtask complete (NF1) or
' restore a completed subtask to incomplete (AF-01). Both paths share the validation (NF2 = AF-01.1),
' the EX-01 check and the final update (NF3 = AF-01.2: record the requested status and recalculate
' parent-task progress), so they merge after the Developer's action.
' Final nodes: F1 = subtask has the requested completion status and parent progress is recalculated
' (postconditions met); F2 = status change rejected, subtask unchanged (EX-01).
!include ../../_shared/activity-style.puml
|DEV| $lane_title("Developer")
|SYS| $lane_title("System")

|DEV|
start
if ($question("Requested status change?")) then ($guard_left("[mark complete]"))
  ' [NF1, TRIGGER, BR-SPRINT-TASK-DEVELOPER]
  :Select incomplete subtask
  and mark it complete;
else ($guard_right("[restore to incomplete", "— AF-01]"))
  ' [AF-01, BR-SPRINT-TASK-DEVELOPER]
  :Restore completed subtask
  to incomplete;
endif
|SYS|
' [NF2, AF-01.1, BR-WORK-ITEM-STATUS]
:Validate requested
status change;
if ($question("Sprint still active?")) then ($guard_left("[active]"))
  ' [NF3, AF-01.2, POST1, POST2]
  :Record requested status and
  recalculate parent-task progress;
  stop
else ($guard_right("[Sprint completed", "— EX-01]"))
  ' [EX-01, BR-SPRINT-TASK-ACTIVE-SPRINT, GUIDE-7.3]
  :Reject subtask status change;
  stop
endif
@enduml
